# Line-ending policy.
# Files that execute on the Linux production server MUST retain LF endings,
# regardless of the committer's OS or core.autocrlf — a CRLF in a shell script
# produces "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" and a broken deploy.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.php      text eol=lf
.htaccess  text eol=lf
